{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
To get the most out of your workout on a stepper, it helps to know the different stepping techniques.

### Step 2
Standard Step: Keep your body upright and step just like you are climbing regular stairs. You can take quick steps at a brisk pace without pushing the pedals all the way to the bottom. This builds endurance and strengthens your glutes and thighs.

### Step 3
Deep / Power Step: Lean your upper body slightly forward from your hips, keep your whole foot flat on each pedal, and push down slowly with power. This increases the load on your glutes and thigh muscles.

### Step 4
Half-Foot Step: Keep your body upright and press the pedals using only the front of your feet (the balls of your feet). Take short, quick steps without pressing the pedals all the way down. This targets your calf muscles and thighs.

{{% /steps %}}
